    "fillOrder": [
      "Day by day and unit by unit, in the order night, day, evening, full-time officers whose rotation has them on that day fill the unit's minimum. Only 12 h officers work nights: those who asked for nights first (most senior first), then the newest. Day and evening go first to officers whose preferred time matches, then by seniority. An 8 h officer keeps one block, day or evening, all quarter.",
      "Every other full-time officer whose rotation has them on that day is then rostered too, even above the minimum, so a full-time officer works their full rotation.",
      "Part-time and casual officers (under 1.0 FTE) then fill what is still short, in their home unit only, newest first, up to their FTE × 80 h in each pay period.",
      "Where a unit is closed on a day, its full-time officers may fill another unit's remaining shortage (by home unit, then seniority).",
      "Every proposed shift is checked by the rules engine (rule set v3) against the officer's last 35 days of shifts: a Block skips that officer, a warning is kept and counted. Planned leave days are never rostered. Anything still short is a gap for a supervisor."
    ]
